      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`Conversation.stop_str` is typed `Union[str, List[str]]`, and several built-in templates use a plain str (phi-4-mm, gme-qwen2-vl, kimi-vl) or a tuple (minicpmv, minicpmo). `_apply_conversation_template` copied that value and then called `.append` or `.extend` to add the request's `stop`. With these templates any chat request that sets `stop` fails with `AttributeError: 'tuple' object has no attribute 'append'` (or the str equivalent), which the server returns as HTTP 500. Some of these templates are chosen from the model path, so a plain `{\"messages\": [...], \"stop\": \"STOP\"}` request breaks on Phi-4-multimodal or MiniCPM-V.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- When the request adds stops, the template stop value becomes a list first (`[stop]` for a str, `list(stop)` for a tuple or list). Then the request stops are added. Requests without `stop` keep the template value unchanged.\n- New unit test `test_request_stop_merges_with_str_and_tuple_template_stop_str`. It renders phi-4-mm and minicpmv with `stop=\"STOP\"` and `stop=[\"A\", \"B\"]` and checks the merged list. Its 4 subtests fail on main with the AttributeError and pass with this change. `test_serving_chat.py` and `test_serving_completions.py` give 177 passed.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot affected. Only the stop list passed to sampling changes, and only for requests that failed before.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot affected.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38032156874](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38032156874)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38032156643](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38032156643)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38032156813](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38032156813)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
